<article class="env-lemma" id="0CTZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CTZ">Lemma <span data-tag="0CTZ">71.2.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $0 \to \mathcal{F}_1 \to \mathcal{F}_2 \to \mathcal{F}_3 \to 0$ be a short exact sequence of quasi-coherent sheaves on $X$. Then $\text{WeakAss}(\mathcal{F}_2) \subset \text{WeakAss}(\mathcal{F}_1) \cup \text{WeakAss}(\mathcal{F}_3)$ and $\text{WeakAss}(\mathcal{F}_1) \subset \text{WeakAss}(\mathcal{F}_2)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For every geometric point $\overline{x} \in X$ the sequence of stalks $0 \to \mathcal{F}_{1, \overline{x}} \to \mathcal{F}_{2, \overline{x}} \to \mathcal{F}_{3, \overline{x}} \to 0$ is a short exact sequence of $\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$-modules. Hence the lemma follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0548" data-tag="0548">10.66.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>